ntinue supporting A. The structured notes say we still need to discuss C and D. So as Agent 1, we should perhaps bring up Candidate C or D, to start covering them, while still maintaining recommendation for A, but note that we need to evaluate them. Provide evidence from our notes: Candidate C can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, but sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. Candidate D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe should connect to prior discussion: \"I agree with A being strong, and note that we still need to evaluate C and D.\" Provide some evidence and perhaps argue that while C has strong anticipation and leadership, his lack of openness to criticism and organization may be concerns. D has strong problem solving and responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership may be concerns. So we still think A is best, but we need to discuss these candidates.\n\nThus public message: agree with A, add that we need to discuss C and D, present some facts, and maintain vote for A.\n\nMetadata JSON: vote Candidate A.\n\nProceed."}
